  partName: Left Front Bolt (3)
  description: The Left Front Bolt (3) is a tiny, complex-shaped bolt located at
    the middle-left-front of the engine, playing a crucial role in securing various
    components together. Its small size belies its importance, as it helps maintain
    the structural integrity of the engine. Interestingly, the bolt's complex shape
    allows it to fit into tight spaces, making it an essential part of the engine's
    overall design.
